#: ../folio-assistant-sci/collab/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:165
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Core's shared review-and-publish process (Process_FolioReviewPublish): the reviewer reads the rendered folio and approves it, asks for changes, or sends a working draft to the Authoring Committee."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/collab/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:105
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Create the folio repository with `bun run cat init-folio` (or the folio_init tool): content/, the document, chapter and first block manifests, the builder shim, AGENTS.md, .mcp.json, the session-start hook and the beans store, with the platform linked rather than copied."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/collab/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:113
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every block edit runs the HCI validation gate — see editing-hci-validation.bpmn."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/collab/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:121
#. Diagram label
msgid "Formalise in Lean"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/collab/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:122
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Give each formal block (definition, theorem, lemma, proposition, corollary, conjecture, proof) a .lean sibling that Lean 4 accepts, in the order lean-formalization sets out. A compiling declaration is not a formalised claim: check vacuity and narrative drift before calling it done, and record the status with proof-verification."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/collab/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:199
#. Diagram label
msgid "green"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/collab/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:20
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "How a scientific paper or book folio is authored end to end, with Lean for its formal claims and LaTeX for its typesetting. Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG. The <bootstrap.processes:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill that implements it; <cat-harness.processes:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared work plan in beans/. Review, publish and committee feedback are core's shared Process_FolioReviewPublish, called after rendering. Its `no` answer, changes asked, comes back to Task_AuthorBlocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/collab/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:50
#. Diagram label
msgid "Lean toolchain (lean-mcp)"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-sci/collab/processes/content/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:66
#. Diagram label
msgid "New paper"
msgstr ""

